 \epsilon.
 \label{eq:first_order_wg_bound}
\end{equation}
Hence, the direct signal leakage from $m'$ to $m$ is
bounded by $\mathcal{O}(\epsilon)$.
Given the modal-selectivity characteristic of each PA, the PA-mediated transition from guided mode $m'$ to $m$ contains at least one undesired transition. Assuming that the considered modal couplings are reciprocal, the direct transition between the PA and its unmatched guided mode $m''$ satisfies
\begin{equation}
 \left|
