 \epsilon.
 \label{eq:first_order_pa_bound}
\end{equation}
Under the higher-order non-resonance assumption, any higher-order coupling path containing at least one undesired modal transition is assumed not to experience appreciable resonant enhancement~\cite{Huang2009CMT}. Therefore, a coupling path containing $o$ undesired transitions preserves the amplitude transfer coefficient of order $\mathcal{O}(\epsilon^o)$. Since the coupling path from $m'$ to $m$ involves at least one undesired modal transition, we have
\begin{equation}
 T_{mm'}(x)
