 (M-1)\epsilon^2
 \right)P_{\text{s}}.
 \label{eq:interference_power_proof}
\end{align}
Therefore, the IMI-to-signal power ratio satisfies
\begin{equation}
 \frac{P_{m}^{\mathrm{I}}}{P_{\text{s}}}=\mathcal{O}\left(\left(M-1\right)\epsilon^2\right), \forall m.
\end{equation}
