\section{Conclusion}
We introduce CORAL, a structured multimodal framework that integrates clinically defined concepts with prompt-driven lesion localization for medical image diagnosis. 
By explicitly modeling structured attributes and spatial grounding within an MLLM, CORAL aligns multimodal reasoning with the coarse-to-fine clinical workflow and enhances interpretability. 
Experiments on BUS and X-ray datasets demonstrate consistent improvements in diagnostic accuracy, concept consistency, and report quality over strong general-purpose and medical MLLMs. 
These results highlight the importance of jointly modeling where abnormalities occur and what attributes support diagnostic decisions for reliable medical AI.




