Fig.~\ref{fig:5} presents the total secrecy rate versus the number of MA elements. Adding more MA elements increases the active array gain and provides additional spatial degrees of freedom for enhancing the legitimate channels, suppressing multiuser interference, and shaping AN toward the eavesdropper. The proposed scheme consistently achieves the highest secrecy rate because the positions of all MA elements are jointly optimized with the active and passive beamforming variables. However, the performance improvement becomes more moderate as the number of MA elements increases, since the available transmit power is shared among more spatial dimensions and the overall performance is also constrained by the finite RIS aperture. These results confirm that the gain provided by additional MA elements can be effectively exploited only when their positions and the remaining transmission variables are properly coordinated.
